    "display_name": "Pancakes",
    "long_instructions": "You are building a neural network for a pancake shop to predict whether pancakes will turn out good or bad, based on the temperature of the pan and how long the pancakes are cooked for.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Open the `pancakes.csv` file and read the data into a variable called `pancakes` that stores a list of rows.\r\n2. Fill in the `TODO`s in the definitions of `inputs` and `outputs` with names of columns from `pancakes.csv`. For the first input, use the pan temperature; for the second input, use the cook time.\r\n3. Fit the model to the training input and output data.\r\n4. Score the model on the test input and output data. Print out the accuracy score.\r\n5. Run the program. Look at the accuracy score, then look at the visualization of the data and what the model learned. How well did the model learn the pattern in the data? You’ll answer a question about this in the next level.\r\n\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nUse `open` to open a file and `csv.DictReader` to read that file into dictionaries.\r\n\r\nUse the `fit` method to train a model and the `score` method to score it. Both methods accept two arguments: a list of inputs and a list of outputs.\r\n",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Evaluate a neural network for a pancake shop to predict whether pancakes will turn out good or bad.",
